			CONTRACT FOR COHABITATION


Articles of Agreement for Cohabitation made on this 20th day of March, 1994.

	Between ______________________
	
	And     ______________________


Residing at: 	______________________

		______________________

The following eight articles of agreement become effective on the date that each
partner signs the bottom line of this contract:

I. Participants of Agreement

This agreement involves only the two partners who sign the bottom line of this
contract. In no way will this contract ever involve third parties, including any
church or government.

II. Primary Agreement

Each partner agrees to:

	1. Develop personal productiveness, integrity, independence, 
	honesty.
                
	2. Seek knowledge, experiences, justice and objective truth 
	through effort, reason and logic.
                
	3. Create and trade values that contribute to the growth and well-
	being of each partner and the relationship.
                
	4. Be monogamous.

	5. Communicate with the other partner.

	6. Allow the other partner his/her own time.

	7. Remain solvent.

	8. Tell the other partner if he/she begins to consider some part of 
	the contract undesirable.

III. Purpose of Agreement

Each partner has carefully chosen the other partner for his/her value.
	
Each partner agrees that his/her selfish purpose in the cohabitation
relationship is to increase the amount of objective values, enjoyment, 
pleasure and happiness available from life. If this purpose is not served 
